   Phantom's own (themes/phantom/CHARACTER.md): a tile is cut paper, the card's plate with its red edge and the
   paperclip corners (G6, G7); pointing throws the red bar in behind the title and resolves it in two cuts, the ink
   flipping to black, and the tile does not move (G15); a press drops it onto its shadow and its face resolves from the
   screen in two cuts (G17); focus stands inside the cut (G16); red is a plate with black ink, never a word: a
   destructive title and a failed name are stamped on the red plate (G5, G8); waiting is the red slash across a halftone
